From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:57:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] batch: prompt reads give way at a chunk boundary on
 every read path (overlapped, one run, pieces, STRATA_PIPED_CONCURRENT) into a
 top-row slot, pinned resume (yslot=), YIELDNO later|final, plan, checkpoint
 and cut carry (opt-in STRATA_READ_YIELD=1, our 6c9607f5 baadb797)

The two production commits as one unit in their final (baadb797) form;
read_yield.hpp and read_yield_test.cpp are production's (3af0006d).

v0.2.12 specifics, all behind read_yield_env() / yield_pin >= 0 / ycarry.on:
- STRATA_PIPED_CONCURRENT: with the switch our hook (should_yield) runs
  instead of stop_at_chunk, the line scan arms through yield_arm, and the
  stop goes through yield_finish in place of upstream's give_way.
- Piece path (STRATA_PIPED_READ_PIECE, batch_read_piece): our block runs
  before give_way and takes the BYIELD.
- One run: through upstream's run() lambda (plan chunks, CPU share gate,
  KVA floor). No hook for a run that co-reads (STRATA_COALESCE_PREFILL).
- park_yield: slot_park_put, then upstream's park_slot (#2526), as BADM
  does. The segment's --prefill-pipe plan goes into partial_plan. A
  not-parked stop hands the plan on as resume_plan, so the re-entry reads
  the same chunks.
- The yield_hook chunk is the plan's chunk when there is one (= C_read).
- The pin also skips upstream's borrow and our borrow_whole. Its
  checkpoints move through move_cks (upstream's general loop), and the
  pin restore carries partial_plan.
- yield_arm also answers final for STRATA_PIPED_MTP, STRATA_KVA and the
  elastic K/V. With piped_mtp, no INFO read_yield line, and one stderr
  line at boot.

